.TH FL-TERM 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-term \- terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-term\fR [\fB\-d\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-T\fR \fITITLE\fR] [\fB\-g\fR \fICOLS\fRx\fIROWS\fR] [\fB\-\-hold\fR] [\fB\-\-scheme\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-e\fR \fICOMMAND\fR...]
.br
\fBfl-term\fR \fB\-\-ssh\fR \fIPROFILE\fR|\fIUSER\fR@\fIHOST\fR[:\fIPORT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A terminal emulator using libvterm. Ctrl+Shift+C/V copy and paste, Shift+PageUp/Down
scroll, Ctrl+plus/minus/0 change the font size. The context menu (right-click) and the menu bar
have the same actions.
.SS Tabs
A window holds several terminals in tabs. Ctrl+Shift+T opens a tab in the current directory,
Ctrl+Shift+W closes the current tab (the last one closes the window), Ctrl+PageUp/PageDown and
Alt+1...9 switch tabs and Ctrl+Shift+PageUp/PageDown move the current tab. In the tab bar a click
on the cross or a middle click closes a tab, the \fB+\fR button or a double click opens one and the
mouse wheel switches tabs. By default the tab bar shows when two or more tabs are open; View >
Show Tabs shows it always or never. Ctrl+Shift+N opens a new window, Ctrl+Shift+Q closes it.
.SS Split panes
Ctrl+Shift+E splits the current terminal side by side, Ctrl+Shift+O one above the other; the new
pane runs a shell in the same directory. Ctrl+Shift+arrows move between panes (a click does too;
a line along the top marks the current one), dragging the gap between two panes resizes them and
Ctrl+Shift+W closes the current pane (the last one closes the tab).
.SS Searching the scrollback
Ctrl+Shift+F opens a search bar at the bottom. Enter (or the up arrow) finds the text further up,
towards older output, Shift+Enter (or the down arrow) further down; the match is selected and
scrolled into view. The search ignores case unless \fBMatch case\fR is on. Escape closes the
bar and goes back to the live screen.
.SS Profiles
A profile is a named way to start a terminal: a command (empty: the shell), a starting folder, a
color scheme and a font size. File > Profiles (or the right-click menu) edits them, opens a tab
with one, and makes one the default for new tabs and windows; \fB\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR
starts a window with it.
.SS Menu bar and preferences
View > Show Menu Bar (Ctrl+Shift+M) shows the File, Edit, View, Tabs, SSH and Help menus.
Edit > Preferences (Ctrl+Shift+P) sets the color scheme, font size, scrollback length, background
opacity, the menu bar and the tab bar. With an opacity below 100% the desktop shows through the
terminal background (text and coloured cells stay opaque); this needs a Wayland session.
.SS SSH
The \fBSSH\fR submenu connects to remote hosts with \fBssh\fR(1) in a new tab.
\fBConnect...\fR (Ctrl+Shift+S) asks for the host, user, port, identity file, jump host (\fB\-J\fR),
port forwards (\fBL\fR \fIport:host:port\fR, \fBR\fR \fIport:host:port\fR, \fBD\fR \fIport\fR; separated by
semicolons), extra ssh options, a remote command and a color scheme to tell the session apart;
it can save the connection under a name. Saved connections and the concrete \fBHost\fR entries of
\fI~/.ssh/config\fR (wildcards skipped, \fBInclude\fR followed) are listed in the submenu for one-click
connecting; \fBManage Connections...\fR edits and deletes saved ones.
Passwords and passphrases are typed in the terminal and never stored; a failed connection keeps
the window open so the error stays readable.
.PP
\fBCopy Public Key to Host...\fR runs \fBssh-copy-id\fR(1), \fBCreate SSH Key...\fR runs
\fBssh-keygen\fR(1) for an Ed25519 key. When \fBsshfs\fR(1) is installed, \fBBrowse Files\fR mounts
a host under \fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/fl-sshfs/\fR and opens it in \fBfl-files\fR(1); the \fBUnmount\fR
submenu lists those mounts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-e COMMAND...\fR
Run COMMAND instead of the shell.
.TP
\fB\-d DIR\fR
Start in DIR.
.TP
\fB\-T TITLE\fR
Fixed window title.
.TP
\fB\-g COLSxROWS\fR
Initial size.
.TP
\fB\-\-hold\fR
Keep the window open after the command exits.
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh PROFILE\fR
Connect to a saved connection, an \fI~/.ssh/config\fR host, or \fIuser\fR@\fIhost\fR[:\fIport\fR].
.TP
\fB\-\-scheme NAME\fR
Color scheme for this window.
.TP
\fB\-\-profile NAME\fR
Start with a saved profile.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/term.ini\fR
[Terminal] \fBColorScheme\fR (dark, light, red, green, blue), \fBFontSize\fR, \fBScrollback\fR,
\fBOpacity\fR (0.2 to 1, background opacity), \fBShowMenuBar\fR (true/false) and \fBShowTabs\fR
(auto, always, never), \fBDefaultProfile\fR. Written by the Preferences dialog and the View menu.
[Profile \fIname\fR] \fBCommand\fR, \fBWorkingDirectory\fR, \fBColorScheme\fR, \fBFontSize\fR,
\fBOpacity\fR: the profiles.
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/ssh.ini\fR
Saved SSH connections, one [Profile \fIname\fR] section each.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBssh\fR(1), \fBssh_config\fR(5), \fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-files\fR(1)
